From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:16:49 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: gsa: Add Tensor G4 (zumapro)

Match google,zumapro-gsa. The 9a's GSA answers the same mailbox and
Trusty hwmgr commands as gs201's, and the driver already leaves the
S2MPU alone when the node has no "s2mpu" range, as a zumapro node
doesn't.

Booted on the Pixel 9a:
7.3.0-rc6-omamobile-tegu-s2mpg15-m1-g991042e2eff3-dirty runs this
driver with only this match added. With it the GSA reports the AoC
inactive, authenticates the signed AoC image and starts it, and the
AoC comes up with its 93 services.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/gsa.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/gsa.c b/drivers/soc/google/gsa.c
index d3e37d182..b491645d6 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/gsa.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/gsa.c
@@ -857,6 +857,7 @@ static void gsa_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct of_device_id gsa_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "google,gs201-gsa" },
+	{ .compatible = "google,zumapro-gsa" },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, gsa_of_match);
